## 21. Supabase Security and RLS

Enable Row Level Security on all tables containing private user information.

Implement policies so:
- Users can view and modify only their own subscriptions.
- Users can view and manage only their own invoices.
- Users can view their own notifications and AI conversation history.
- Users can access only their own integration settings and webhook configuration.
- Approved global templates can be read by authorized users.
- Only authorized administrators can approve, reject, or suspend accounts.
- Ordinary users cannot grant themselves admin roles.
- Approval status cannot be changed by an ordinary user.
- Private Storage objects can be accessed only by authorized owners and administrators where appropriate.
- Sensitive admin operations run through trusted server-side authorization.

Do not assume authentication alone provides authorization.

Test the policies using separate normal-user, pending-user, and admin accounts.

Never disable RLS merely to make the frontend work.

## 22. Subscription Calculations

Implement a shared, tested financial calculation module.

Calculate:
- Active monthly recurring cost.
- Annualized recurring cost.
- Total by original currency.
- Total in selected display currency.
- Spending by category.
- Next 7-day renewal amount.
- Next 30-day renewal amount.
- Potential savings based on explicit assumptions.

For weekly billing, use a documented annualization convention. For quarterly and half-yearly billing, normalize by the number of billing periods per year. Handle custom intervals explicitly.

Exclude cancelled and expired subscriptions from future recurring totals as appropriate. Treat free trials and paused subscriptions according to clearly defined rules.

For mixed currencies, convert only when a valid exchange rate exists. Never add ₹1,000 and $20 as though they were the same currency.

Ensure all totals remain consistent across dashboard cards, tables, reports, and AI summaries.

